### Make sure the server is running first (run main.go)

### 1. Create a task
POST http://localhost:8080/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Preview PR"}

### 2. Create another task
POST http://localhost:8080/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Write release notes"}

### 3. List all tasks
GET http://localhost:8080/tasks

### 4. Mark id=1 as complete
PUT http://localhost:8080/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Preview PR", "status": 1}

### 5. Delete id=2
DELETE http://localhost:8080/tasks/2

### 6. Error: update a task that does not exist → 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/tasks/999
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "x"}

### 7. Error: empty name and invalid status → 400 VALIDATION_FAILED, with both fields listed in details
POST http://localhost:8080/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "", "status": 5}

### 8. Send X-Trace-Id: the response's X-Trace-Id and the error's trace_id reuse my-trace-123
PUT http://localhost:8080/tasks/999
Content-Type: application/json
X-Trace-Id: my-trace-123

{"name": "x"}

### 9. Error: wrong method → 405 METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED, with the allowed methods in the Allow header
DELETE http://localhost:8080/tasks
